Falsifies `calendar::verification::the_unix_format_fits_any_i64`.

The defect: `Writer::signed` sizes its digit scratch at 18 bytes. An `i64` has up to 19 digits, so the nineteenth
write runs off the end of the array.

Expected to fail: the bounds check on `digits[n]` inside `Writer::signed`, reached through the harness's `w.signed(secs)`.

